    "intro_html":  "Sauerbraten is the German sweet and sour pot roast, and the gravy is thickened with crushed gingersnap cookies. That is not a gimmick, it is how it has been done for centuries, and it produces a sauce nothing else quite matches. The vinegar marinade does the tenderizing before the slow cooker even starts. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e29 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 564 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.30\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
